/ item-doors 62/63: a goal's type is the plain goal type, not the app's node. %!app.goal.type.name% is goal, and a goal's
/ %g!type% written is the goal type's face (goal). Red before: Replace swapped the type list's own goal entry for the app's
/ node, so asking a goal what type it is answered the node (the dump of every goal), not goal.
GoalIsOfTypeGoal
- assert.equals(Expected="goal", Actual=%!app.goal.type.name%, Message="the running goal is of type goal")
- set %g% = %!app.goal["GoalIsOfTypeGoal"]%
- set %shown% = "type: %g!type%"
- assert.equals(Expected="type: goal", Actual=%shown%, Message="a goal's type, written, is goal")
